NODE id=matrix/executor/cmd/mcl-e2e.coerceArg kind=func
  digest=b3:f7551527d8e1b21dfd4dd2601831f17ee6a98c0f16bbf802eb77ea667751c205 file=executor/cmd/mcl-e2e/walk.go range=244:279 lang=go exported=false byte_range=7738:8656
  sig=func coerceArg(v string) interface{}
  doc=coerceArg converts a string-typed PlanTree arg into its likely\nJSON-friendly type. The IR shape is map[string]string for canonical\nhashing simplicity; MCP servers expect ints/bools per their input\nschemas. The walker does best-effort coercion: pure-digit strings\nbecome int, "true"/"false" become bool, everything else stays string.\n\nA future plan-IR revision may add typed Args (oneof string/int/bool/\nnumber/array) at which point this becomes a no-op shim.
EDGES
  ^defines=matrix/executor/cmd/mcl-e2e/walk.go

